    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Fenelon Properties are delighted to bring to the market 21 Killadreenan, a charming three-bedroom extended semi-detached cottage occupying a particularly attractive position within this established residential area of Newtownmountkennedy.\r\n\r\nExtending to approximately 71 sq.m. (764 sq.ft.), No. 21 is a characterful property which now offers an excellent opportunity for a purchaser to modernise and create a home to their own taste. While in need of updating, the property provides well-proportioned and flexible accommodation together with a particularly long and mature rear garden, which is undoubtedly one of its standout features.\r\nThe accommodation comprises an entrance porch and foyer, living room, three bedrooms, dining room, kitchen, rear hall and shower room. The traditional cottage-style façade, tall windows and mature front garden give the property considerable charm and kerb appeal.\r\nOutside, the property is approached through wrought-iron gates with a paved driveway providing off-street parking. Mature hedging and planting create an attractive and private setting to the front.\r\n\r\nTo the rear lies a generous and mature garden extending well beyond the immediate rear of the house. Mainly laid in lawn and bordered by mature trees, shrubs and hedging, the garden enjoys an attractive outlook towards the surrounding countryside and hills. Given the generous proportions of the site, the property offers excellent scope to extend and further enhance the existing accommodation, subject to the necessary planning permission.\r\n\r\nThe property benefits from oil-fired central heating and mains services.\r\nKilladreenan is a mature and convenient residential location within easy reach of Newtownmountkennedy village, where a good selection of shops, cafés, schools and everyday amenities are available. The N11/M11 is also readily accessible, providing excellent connectivity to Greystones, Bray, Dublin and further afield.\r\n\r\nNo. 21 represents a particularly appealing opportunity for first-time buyers, downsizers, renovators or purchasers looking for a character property with a substantial garden and the scope to put their own stamp on a home."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Foyer – 1.98m x 1.44m\r\nWelcoming entrance area providing access to the living room and adjoining accommodation. Carpet.\r\nLiving Room – 3.74m x 3.58m\r\nBright reception room positioned to the front of the property, featuring a traditional fireplace and twin front-facing bay windows. Laid with carpet.\r\nBedroom 1 – 2.95m x 3.00m\r\nDouble bedroom positioned to the front of the property with two windows overlooking the front garden. Carpet. \r\nBedroom 2 – 3.18m x 2.64m\r\nWell-proportioned bedroom with front-facing windows. Carept.\r\nBedroom 3 – 3.74m x 2.07m\r\nLocated towards the centre/rear of the property and suitable for use as a bedroom, home office or additional reception space if desired.\r\nDining Room – 3.18m x 3.72m\r\nLocated at the heart of the home with fireplace and access through to the kitchen. Access to hot press. Timber floor.\r\nKitchen – 2.82m x 3.06m\r\nFitted kitchen with a good range of timber eye and floor-level units, contrasting worktops and tiled splashback. Stainless steel sink unit, space and plumbing for appliances, gas cooker, tiled flooring and dual-aspect windows overlooking the rear garden.\r\nRear Hall – 1.99m x 0.96m\r\nProviding access to the shower room and rear of the property.\r\nShower Room – 1.98m x 1.99m\r\nComprising shower, WC and wash-hand basin.\r\nOutside.\r\nThe property is approached through wrought-iron gates onto a paved driveway with off-street parking. Mature hedging, lawns and established planting provide an attractive setting to the front.\r\nA major feature of No. 21 is the long rear garden, which offers a substantial amount of outdoor space and is mainly laid in lawn with mature trees, hedging and planting throughout. The elevated surroundings provide pleasant views towards the Wicklow countryside and hills.\r\n\r\n* Please note we have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. All measurements are approximate, and photographs/ floorplans provide for guidance only*."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Charming 3-bedroom extended semi-detached cottage\r\nCharacterful cottage-style façade.\r\nApprox. 71 sq.m. / 764 sq.ft.\r\nExcellent blank canvas in need of modernisation.\r\nParticularly long and mature rear garden.\r\nAttractive views towards the surrounding countryside and hills.\r\nOff-street parking behind wrought-iron gates.\r\nOil-fired central heating & Mains services.\r\n Convenient to Newtownmountkennedy village and local amenities.\r\n Easy access to the N11/M11."
      },
